{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 25, :comments ["<b>And behold, she is Leah.</b> Our Rabbis of blessed memory darshaned: was she not Leah until now? Rather, Jacob had conveyed signs to Rachel, and when she saw that they were bringing Leah in to him, she said, 'now my sister will be shamed'; so she rose and gave her the signs. Rachel grasped the spindle of silence; Leah grasped the spindle of thanksgiving. Rachel grasped the spindle of silence — for Jacob would send her gifts (סבלונות) and Laban would take them from her and give them to Leah, and Rachel was silent; therefore all her children were possessors of silence: for Benjamin knew of the sale of Joseph and was silent. Saul, her grandson's son — what is written of him? (I Samuel 10:16) ״ואת דבר המלוכה לא הגיד לו״. Esther — what is written of her? (Esther 2:20) ״אין אסתר מגדת מולדתה ואת עמה״. Leah grasped the spindle of thanksgiving — she said, ״הפעם אודה את ה׳״; therefore all her children were possessors of thanksgiving: Judah — what is written of him? (Genesis 49:8) ״יהודה אתה יודוך אחיך״. David said (Psalms 136:1) ״הודו לה' כי טוב״. Daniel — it is written of him (Daniel 6:11) ״ומצלא ומודא קדם אלהיה״."], :book :genesis, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 29, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:16:20.980200846Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}